# Testing Standards

## Mandatory Integration Tests (AC-17, AC-18)

All must pass before release. Location: `server/tests/integration/`

| Scenario | Expected |
| -------- | -------- |
| Open→In Progress | 200 |
| In Progress→Resolved | 200 |
| Resolved→Closed | 200 |
| Open→Cancelled | 200 |
| In Progress→Cancelled | 200 |
| Open→Resolved (skip) | 400 |
| Open→Closed (skip) | 400 |
| Resolved→Open (revert) | 400 |
| Closed→any (terminal) | 400 |
| Cancelled→any (terminal) | 400 |
| `PATCH /tickets/:id` with `status` field | 400 `STATUS_NOT_ALLOWED_HERE` |
| `GET /tickets?status=Invalid` | 400 |
| `POST /tickets` without title | 400 |
| `GET /tickets/99999` | 404 |

## Test Rules

- After **any** status logic change — run `npm run test` in `server/` before committing
- Never bypass failing tests — fix the root cause; fix the test only if the test itself is wrong
- Use a separate `DATABASE_URL` for tests or truncate tables between runs
- Test command: `cd server && npm run test`

## Performance (no dedicated test suite needed — apply during implementation)

- Use Prisma `include` for related data — avoid N+1 on list and detail endpoints
- Debounce search input before firing API calls
- Avoid inline object/array creation inside render loops
- Full list return is acceptable for exercise dataset — no pagination required in v1
- Cache users list per session where sensible — users list is read-only seed data
